#!/usr/bin/env ruby

def normalize(value)
  value.downcase.gsub(/[^a-z0-9]/, '')
end

DEFINITIONS = {
  "Kidney Pain vs. Back Pain" => "Kidney pain is usually felt in the flank beneath the ribs and may accompany urinary symptoms, fever, nausea, or blood in the urine. Back pain more often changes with movement or position; severe pain, fever, weakness, or urinary change needs assessment.",
  "Knee and Ankle Pain After Hip Replacement" => "Knee or ankle pain after hip replacement may reflect altered gait and muscle loading, nerve irritation, swelling, a stress injury, infection, or a blood clot. New severe pain, calf swelling, fever, wound drainage, or breathlessness requires prompt evaluation.",
  "Knee Bursitis" => "Knee bursitis is inflammation of a fluid-filled sac around the knee, causing localized swelling, tenderness, and pain with kneeling or movement. Repetitive pressure, trauma, arthritis, gout, or infection can contribute; fever or redness requires urgent review.",
  "Knee Injury and Meniscus Tears" => "A meniscus tear is damage to the cartilage cushion between the thighbone and shinbone, often after twisting or with degeneration. Pain, swelling, catching, or locking may occur; treatment ranges from rehabilitation to surgery according to tear, symptoms, and stability.",
  "Knee Pain Facts" => "Knee pain can arise from ligament or meniscus injury, arthritis, bursitis, tendon disease, gout, infection, nerve disease, or referred hip or spine pain. Deformity, inability to bear weight, fever, a locked joint, or sudden swelling needs assessment.",
  "Kyphosis vs Lordosis Differences and Similarities" => "Kyphosis is excessive backward curvature of the upper spine, while lordosis is excessive inward curvature, usually in the lower spine. Both may be postural or structural and can result from growth disorders, fractures, degeneration, or muscle imbalance.",
